---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import koreaGroup from '../assets/images/korea-robotics-teaching-group-photo.jpeg';
import koreaHike from '../assets/images/korea-hike-mountain-summit-victory-pose.jpeg';
---

<section id="teaching">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="section-label">Teaching & Speaking</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Passing it on</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Robotics stuck with Karl partly because people took the time to teach it to him well, so
      he has tried to return the favor.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-row">
      <div class="feature-photos">
        <figure class="tall">
          <Image src={koreaGroup} alt="Karl with a large group of Korean high school students at Hansung Science High School, all making a finger-heart gesture" width={800} height={1000} />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image src={koreaHike} alt="Karl with fists raised on a mountain summit near Seoul, radar dome visible in the background" width={800} height={600} />
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-text">
        <h3>A week of robotics in Korea</h3>
        <p>
          In July 2025, Karl taught a week-long robotics program to high schoolers at Hansung
          Science High School (한성과학고등학교) in Korea, guiding students through Arduino-based
          projects from first principles. He stayed on afterward for some hiking around Seoul.
          A nearby summit with a radar dome, likely Bukhansan, capped off the trip.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="origin-story" style="margin-top: 3.5rem; max-width: 70ch;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Telling the Möbius story at MIT Sloan</h3>
      <p>
        At the end of September 2026, Karl went back to campus to speak with the MIT Sloan
        Robotics Club about Möbius Industries, covering the business, the technology, and what
        it is actually like to go from a three-month favor for a friend to running AI, sensing,
        and software for a funded robotics startup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
